<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ulf Jarl</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1026</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Ulf Thorgilsson, Earl Ulf</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ulf Thorgilsson, known as Ulf Jarl, was a Danish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jarl">jarl</a> of Skåne and regent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>, the father of King Sweyn II and so the progenitor of the House of Estridsen, which ruled Denmark from 1047 to 1375. He took part in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cnut-the-great">Cnut the Great</a>'s invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1016 and married Cnut's sister Estrid; from about 1024 he governed Denmark as Cnut's regent and guardian of Cnut's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harthacnut">Harthacnut</a>. In 1026 he persuaded the freemen to elect Harthacnut king, a ruse that would have made him ruler, and the sources disagree on his side around the Battle of the Helgeå. After a quarrel over chess, Cnut had him killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roskilde">Roskilde</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christmas">Christmas</a> 1026.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ulf-jarl.jpg" alt="Ulf Jarl" width="330" height="487" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Drawing by M. Meredith Williams · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KingCanute_and_EarlUlf.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>And at Roskilde, at Christmas 1026, Cnut the Great had his regent and brother-in-law <b>Ulf Jarl</b> killed after a quarrel over chess.</blockquote><a href="/essays/christmas-day-in-history">Christmas Day in History</a></li><li><blockquote>In Denmark the jarl was the king’s deputy, as <b>Ulf Jarl</b> was to Cnut the Great, and when Cnut conquered England he made Eric of Lade earl of Northumbria.</blockquote><a href="/societies/vikings">Social Hierarchy of the Vikings</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roskilde">Roskilde</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/denmark">Denmark</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=55.64,12.08&amp;year=1016" aria-label="Roskilde on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4814 266 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Ulf Jarl"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5264 536h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5264 536h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=55.64,12.08&amp;year=1016">What was here in 1016? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
